%%{init: {'fontFamily':'Inter, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'}}%%
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB

    state "Ingress list" as Ingress
    state "Popped by a worker" as Popped
    state "Links running" as Links
    state "Wrap-up, egress then storage" as WrapUp
    state "Ingress DLQ, DLQ:#lt;ingress_list#gt;" as IngressDLQ
    state "Storage DLQ, DLQ:storage:#lt;backend#gt;" as StorageDLQ
    state "Skipped by hook" as Skipped
    state "Halted by a link" as Halted
    state "Saved to the backend" as Saved
    state "Manual recovery, error logged" as Manual

    [*] --> Ingress : RPUSH from API or follower
    Ingress --> Popped : BLPOP by a worker
    Popped --> Ingress : shutdown requested, LPUSH to head
    Popped --> Skipped : before_processing returns falsy
    Popped --> IngressDLQ : before_processing raises
    Popped --> Links : chain starts
    Links --> Halted : a link returns falsy
    Links --> WrapUp : every link returns an id
    Links --> IngressDLQ : exception in a link, hook or tracer
    WrapUp --> IngressDLQ : egress enqueue raises
    WrapUp --> Saved : backend save returns
    WrapUp --> StorageDLQ : backend save raises
    WrapUp --> Manual : dead-letter fails, body missing or Redis error
    IngressDLQ --> Ingress : POST /dlq/reprocess, LPOP then RPUSH, whole chain runs again
    StorageDLQ --> Saved : POST /dlq/storage/reprocess, write only, see D09
    StorageDLQ --> StorageDLQ : retry fails, entry stays
    Skipped --> [*]
    Halted --> [*]
    Saved --> [*]

    note right of IngressDLQ
        EXPIRE resets the
        body TTL to the
        DLQ expiry setting
        unless that is 0.
        GET /dlq only reads.
    end note

    note right of StorageDLQ
        One entry per
        failed backend.
        A longer TTL or a
        persistent body
        stays as it is.
    end note
